{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_001", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0003"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0003_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Colorectal cancer is the third leading cause of cancer-\nrelated deaths among men and women in the United\nStates, with 151,030 new cases estimated to have occured\nin 2022. “Colorectal cancer” can refer to any cancer that\nforms in the tissue that lines the inside of the colon or\nrectum. While some people are at higher risk than others,\nanyone can get colorectal cancer. Screening is important\nto detect the disease and remove precancerous polyps\nbefore they become cancerous.", "semantic_text": "Colorectal cancer is the third leading cause of cancer-related deaths among men and women in the United States, with 151,030 new cases estimated to have occured in 2022. “Colorectal cancer” can refer to any cancer that forms in the tissue that lines the inside of the colon or rectum. While some people are at higher risk than others, anyone can get colorectal cancer. Screening is important to detect the disease and remove precancerous polyps before they become cancerous.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0003_geometry", "bbox": [92, 427, 593, 651], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0003"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_002", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0005"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0005_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "The following symptoms can be caused by other\nconditions, but people experiencing them should\nconsult their doctor:", "semantic_text": "The following symptoms can be caused by other conditions, but people experiencing them should consult their doctor:", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0005_geometry", "bbox": [92, 728, 523, 804], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0005"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_003", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0006"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0006_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "■ Diarrhea or constipation\n■ A feeling that your bowel does not empty completely\n■ Blood in your stool\n■ Stools that are narrower than usual\n■ Frequent gas pains or cramps\n■ Frequently feeling full or bloated\n■ Weight loss with no known reason\n■ Fatigue\n■ Nausea or vomiting", "semantic_text": "■ Diarrhea or constipation ■ A feeling that your bowel does not empty completely ■ Blood in your stool ■ Stools that are narrower than usual ■ Frequent gas pains or cramps ■ Frequently feeling full or bloated ■ Weight loss with no known reason ■ Fatigue ■ Nausea or vomiting", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0006_geometry", "bbox": [92, 808, 560, 1068], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0006"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_004", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0008"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0008_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "While anyone can get colorectal cancer, the National\nCancer Institute (NCI) reports that slightly more than\n1 in 25 men and women will develop colorectal cancer in\ntheir lifetime.", "semantic_text": "While anyone can get colorectal cancer, the National Cancer Institute (NCI) reports that slightly more than 1 in 25 men and women will develop colorectal cancer in their lifetime.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0008_geometry", "bbox": [92, 1119, 587, 1223], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0008"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_005", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0009"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0009_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "People who have had colorectal cancer in the past or\nwho have had certain kinds of colorectal polyps removed\nare at greater risk for developing colorectal cancer, as are\nthose with a family history of the disease. People with\nLynch syndrome or familial adenomatous polyposis, both\nof which are inherited conditions, or who have a history\nof inflammatory bowel disease such as ulcerative colitis or\nCrohn's disease are also at higher risk.", "semantic_text": "People who have had colorectal cancer in the past or who have had certain kinds of colorectal polyps removed are at greater risk for developing colorectal cancer, as are those with a family history of the disease. People with Lynch syndrome or familial adenomatous polyposis, both of which are inherited conditions, or who have a history of inflammatory bowel disease such as ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease are also at higher risk.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0009_geometry", "bbox": [92, 1223, 589, 1423], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0009"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_006", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0010"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0010_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Some lifestyle factors associated with increased risk\ninclude excessive alcohol consumption, obesity, smoking,\nand possibly diet.", "semantic_text": "Some lifestyle factors associated with increased risk include excessive alcohol consumption, obesity, smoking, and possibly diet.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0010_geometry", "bbox": [92, 1423, 583, 1499], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0010"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_007", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0012"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0012_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Rates of colorectal cancer are also higher for Black people\nand non-Hispanic American Indians/Alaska Natives than any\nother racial or ethnic groups.", "semantic_text": "Rates of colorectal cancer are also higher for Black people and non-Hispanic American Indians/Alaska Natives than any other racial or ethnic groups.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0012_geometry", "bbox": [634, 427, 1151, 502], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0012"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_008", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0013"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0013_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "As you get older, your risk increases. The U.S. Preventive\nServices Task Force recommends colorectal cancer\nscreening for adults ages 45 to 75 of average risk. Screening\nfor patients ages 76 to 85 is recommended for select\nindividuals. Colorectal cancer is still rare among adults\nyounger than 50, but these rates are increasing. You should\nconsult your doctor about screening methods and frequency.", "semantic_text": "As you get older, your risk increases. The U.S. Preventive Services Task Force recommends colorectal cancer screening for adults ages 45 to 75 of average risk. Screening for patients ages 76 to 85 is recommended for select individuals. Colorectal cancer is still rare among adults younger than 50, but these rates are increasing. You should consult your doctor about screening methods and frequency.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0013_geometry", "bbox": [634, 502, 1153, 677], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0013"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2_18_HY_009", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0015"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0015_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Colorectal cancer is detected using a range of procedures,\nsome invasive and some not. These include colonoscopies,\nstool tests, and sigmoidoscopies. Abnormalities, including\nlesions or polyps found during a screening, will be tested\nfor cancer. A new approach is to check blood samples for\ngenetic material that polyps or tumors may release into the\nbloodstream.", "semantic_text": "Colorectal cancer is detected using a range of procedures, some invasive and some not. These include colonoscopies, stool tests, and sigmoidoscopies. Abnormalities, including lesions or polyps found during a screening, will be tested for cancer. A new approach is to check blood samples for genetic material that polyps or tumors may release into the bloodstream.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0015_geometry", "bbox": [634, 729, 1136, 904], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0015"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_58/hybrid/real_065_batch_60_Volume_17_Issue_2/page_0018/decisions.json"}
